  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a permutation PPP of length NNN.\n\nFor each 1≤i≤N1\\le i \\le N1≤i≤N, find the number of subarrays of PPP with sum iii.\n\nNote that a permutation of length NNN consists of all integers from 111 to NNN exactly once.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains a positive integer NNN −-− the length of PPP.\nThe second line contains NNN space separated distinct integers, P1,P2…PNP_1, P_2 \\ldots P_NP1​,P2​…PN​ −-− denoting the permutation PPP.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, NNN space-separated integers, where the ithi^{th}ith integer denotes the number of subarrays with sum iii.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Pi≤N1 \\leq P_i \\leq N1≤Pi​≤N",
      "Pi≠PjP_i \\neq P_jPi​=Pj​ if i≠ji \\neq ji=j",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n1\n2\n1 2\n3\n3 1 2",
        "output": "1\n1 1\n1 1 2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The only subarray is [1][1][1] with sum 111.\nTest case 222:\n\nFor sum 111, the only possible subarray is [1][1][1].\nFor sum 222, the only possible subarray is [2][2][2].\n\nTest case 333:\n\nFor sum 111, the only possible subarray is [1][1][1].\nFor sum 222, the only possible subarray is [2][2][2].\nFor sum 333, the possible subarrays are [3][3][3] and [1,2][1, 2][1,2]."
      }
    ]
  },
